WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
<b><font color='#000000'>If you want to make your data available in the long term, </font></b>

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.041
<b><font color='#000000'>you need to add some metadata to your data </font></b>

3
00:00:05.041 --> 00:00:07.291
<b><font color='#000000'>before you can move on to archiving.</font></b>

4
00:00:07.291 --> 00:00:10.250
<b><font color='#000000'>Because descriptive metadata is an important aspect </font></b>

5
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:13.541
<b><font color='#000000'>that enables the reuse of your data in the future.</font></b>

6
00:00:13.541 --> 00:00:17.416
<b><font color='#000000'>In the FDOrganizer you can add metadata at different levels. </font></b>

7
00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:20.500
<b><font color='#000000'>You can specify metadata for your entire project, </font></b>

8
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.625
<b><font color='#000000'>as well as for each folder or individual file. </font></b>

9
00:00:23.625 --> 00:00:26.291
<b><font color='#000000'>If you want to add metadata at the file level,</font></b>

10
00:00:26.291 --> 00:00:29.416
<b><font color='#000000'>first select your package to view the files inside,</font></b>

11
00:00:29.416 --> 00:00:32.750
<b><font color='#000000'>then you can use the book symbol next to each file.</font></b>

12
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.458
<b><font color='#000000'>If you want to add metadata for the whole project, </font></b>

13
00:00:35.458 --> 00:00:38.125
<b><font color='#000000'> use the book symbol next to the projects name. </font></b>

